# Real-World Example 3: Grade Calculator

```python
def get_grade(marks):

    if marks >= 90:
        return "A+"
    elif marks >= 75:
        return "A"
    elif marks >= 60:
        return "B"
    elif marks >= 35:
        return "C"
    else:
        return "Fail"

grade = get_grade(82)

print(grade)
```

Output:

```text
A
```

